{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Got your vitals while he finishes typing. Blood pressure is one twenty-eight over eighty-two, pulse seventy-six, temperature thirty-six point eight, oxygen sat ninety-nine percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, this screen froze again. Uh, what are we seeing you for?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): Um. There's a lump on my neck. It doesn't hurt or anything.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Say that once more? I was in the wrong chart.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Right side of my neck. A lump. Painless. Been there three weeks. I don't know, doctor, it just showed up.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'm his brother, I stay with him. He's lost weight, you can see it, his cheeks are hollow.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): The lump part, yeah, but I have not lost weight. I don't know, doctor, he's wrong about that.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Does the lump hurt when you touch it?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Not now. No fever.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any night sweats?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): One night. I woke up sweaty just once. I don't know if that even counts.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Swallowing okay? Sore throat?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Throat's been fine.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): And breathing, cough, your chest, anything there?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Of. Nothing.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): Oh. My cat scratched me. Left hand. I don't know when, doctor, maybe a couple weeks ago? It's healed.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (CAREGIVER): The cat's name is Pickles. He sleeps on the router. Sorry, not helpful.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me feel. Right. About 2 centimeters on the right side of the neck, it moves, not tender. Throat looks clear. The scratch on the left hand is closed over, healed.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Medicines? Wait, I clicked out of the chart. Go through them again.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Amladipine for the pressure, I almost said ten milligrams but it's five, in the morning. The cholesterol one at night, twenty milligrams, I don't know the name, doctor. Sugar tablets, metforman, five hundred twice a day. And only the ayurvedic powder in the morning, half a teaspoon.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Five of amlodipine mornings, cholesterol tablet twenty at night, metformin 500 twice daily, powder in the morning. Not changing any of that.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): My working thought is a reactive lymph node, maybe tied to that cat scratch. Not a final diagnosis. I can't be sure from this.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): So is it serious? I don't know.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): We'll know more from tests. The nurse takes bloods Thursday morning, a CBC and a chemistry panel. Don't fast. Take your usual morning pills.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): And I'll book a neck ultrasound for Monday afternoon.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): If those are borderline we do the third test, Bartonella titers. If the lump does not settle, we might do a CT. Not setting that up today.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (CAREGIVER): You want him to drop the powder or not?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): I didn't say stop it. I'll see you in two weeks, let's see the results then.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (NURSE): Thursday eight thirty for the draw, no fasting. Ultrasound desk will call about Monday.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): If it blows up fast or you get a fever, call us. Otherwise I'll see you in two weeks."
 ],
